<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis outsources infotech to IBM.</title>
<headline>Novartis outsources infotech to IBM.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss life sciences group Novartis AG said it would transfer its information technology activities into a joint venture that will be majority-owned by U.S. computer firm IBM.</p>
<p>Later the venture will become an independent business unit of IBM, Novartis said, noting the move would affect some 300 Novartis employees.  </p>
<p>The 300 employees will continue to be employed in Basle.</p>
<p>Novartis' activities that are being outsourced include its computer centre, network management, application development and maintenance.</p>
<p>The venture will start operating on July 1.</p>
<p>IBM plans to build up an information centre in Basle which will offer information services to other customers.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
